From 10a7f6061a69177bdbe275d095b856a34a6298bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corey <coreysho@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 04:49:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Karil fires with OSRS's crossbow animation

And the other five brothers keep theirs, because they already are OSRS's.

THE MEASUREMENT FIRST. Both caches decoded and compared frame by frame - OSRS's
seq configs out of caches/newest cache with tools/models/osrsseq.py, the 377
cache's out of all.seq:

  Ahrim   quarterstaff 2078   12 frames / 43 ticks  vs OSRS 12 / 43  identical
  Dharok  slash 2066           9 / 26               vs OSRS  9 / 26  identical
  Guthan  war spear 2082      14 / 35               vs OSRS 14 / 35  identical
  Torag   crush 2068          11 / 36               vs OSRS 11 / 36  identical
  Verac   2067                11 / 31               vs OSRS 11 / 31  identical
  Karil   crossbow 2075        7 / 48               vs OSRS 22 / 69  DIFFERENT

Not just the totals - every delay matches element for element. Five of the six
are already the OSRS animation, and importing them would have been strictly
worse than doing nothing (see the skeleton, below).

The trap in that comparison is worth recording: the 377 attack seqs carry no
delay= lines at all, so a naive read says they have no timing. They do -
SeqType reads a delay of 0 and falls back to the FRAME's own baked delay, and
only then to 1 tick. That is the RS2 design: timing lives in the frame data,
and OSRS moved it into the seq. So the comparison had to read the baked delays
out of the .anim sets in models/, which is what turned "five animations have no
timing" into "five animations match OSRS exactly".

WHAT WAS IMPORTED. OSRS seqs 2074-2077 - ready, fire, walk, run - as four
.anim sets, 43 frames, and a generated
scripts/skill_combat/configs/ranged/osrs_crossbow_anims.seq.

Only fire actually differs; the other three came across because of the
SKELETON. The client only walk-merges two frames built on the same base
(Model.java: "if (!sameSkeleton(...)) { applyTransform(arg2); return; }"), and
an OSRS-converted frame carries the OSRS player base - framemap 0, 245
transform groups - where a 377 one carries the 117-group 377 base. An OSRS fire
merged against a 377 walk drops one of the two, so the four have to share a
base.

Five crossbows, not one: the pristine item and the four degrade states. There
is a sixth obj, barrows_karil_weapon_broken, which carries no iop2=Wield and no
animation at all because a fully degraded crossbow cannot be held - the first
version of the battery check counted to five and went red on it, which is how
that exclusion came to be stated rather than assumed.

The NPC gets the fire and nothing else. His readyanim and walkanim stay the
cache's 377 ones: they only matter to the walk-merge, and the merge only
happens while an animation is playing AND he is moving, which a shooting npc
never is.

THE BOLT RACK NEEDED NOTHING. It is already in the cache as
[barrows_karil_ammo], name "Bolt rack", and the cache gives it
param=proj_travel,crossbowbolt_travel itself - so that is the ammunition's own
statement of what it looks like in flight, not a substitution. A previous note
claiming otherwise was wrong. The battery now pins Karil's projectile to the
bolt rack's so the two cannot drift.

And one thing that looked wrong and is not: Verac's flail attacking with
something called barrow_dharok_crush is the CACHE's own choice -
[barrows_verac_weapon] carries crushattack_anim,barrow_dharok_crush in all.obj.
The seq's name is the unpacker's label.

tools/pose377.py is new, and is the half of the preview that was missing.
tools/models/posepreview.py poses an OSRS mesh with an OSRS animation; it
cannot say whether a CONVERTED animation looks right on the mesh this server
animates. That mattered here: over the 117 groups the two player skeletons
share, the transform types all match but the vertex-label lists differ in 63 of
them. This reads what the build reads - a .anim set, which carries both the
frames and their base - applies the transforms the way the client does, and
renders. No cache, no importer, no laptop. Karil posed clean on it.

Verification: clean build; rs2check 1703 scripts / 493 configs, 0 ERROR 0
CHECK; tools/barrows_battery.py 917 checks (852 before), the new group comparing
every number against tools/karilanimspec.json, which was written by decoding
BOTH caches before any of it was imported; tools/barrows_mutate.py 218
mutations, every one caught by its own check.

Two of those checks were strengthened after a mutation walked through them: a
priority check that asked whether the right value appeared anywhere in the
block passed when a second priority line was added above it, and the same for
a duplicated rangeattack_anim. Both now count the lines. A third mutation was
mis-anchored - param=proj_travel,crossbowbolt_travel is on three npcs in
all.npc and the unanchored version edited one of the other two.

